course: dictionary
lesson: 8334
title: Romance: love, stories and excitement
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Romance has more than one meaning, so use the words around it to find the right one. In «Most TV romances end after the show», romances are stories about people falling in love. The word «show» is a clue that this is about a story on screen.
explain: Romance can also mean a loving relationship between two people, or the feeling of love and excitement inside that relationship. Ask yourself who is involved and what is happening. If two people are in love, romance means that loving relationship.
explain: «The romance of travel» is different. Nobody is falling in love there. It means the exciting, mysterious feeling you get about going to new places. Try your meaning in the sentence: «the exciting, mysterious feeling of travel» still makes sense.
explain: The sentence also gives a clue: real relationships take much longer than a few weeks of filming. So TV romances are often quick and neat, but real love takes time. Cinderella is a famous fairy tale romance that many children know.
fact: Romance means a loving relationship between two people, or the feeling of love and excitement in it.
fact: A romance can also be a story or film about love, such as a romance novel.
fact: «The romance of the sea» means the exciting, mysterious feeling about the sea, not a love story.
fact: «A holiday romance» is a short love story between two people on holiday.
fact: Romance can be a verb too, but it is old-fashioned, so you will rarely hear it today.
exercise: «Most TV romances end after the show; real relationships take much longer than a few weeks of filming.» What does romances mean here? | Television sets that break | *Stories about people falling in love | Arguments between friends | Long walks by the sea
exercise: Maya says, «The romance of the sea kept me dreaming.» What does romance mean here? | A loving couple who live by the sea | *An exciting, mysterious feeling about the sea | A cold, wet day on the coast
exercise: What is a holiday romance? | A holiday with lots of rain | A list of things to pack | A long journey by train | *A short love story between two people on holiday
test: In «a romance novel», what is a romance? | A list of facts about animals | A book of maps | A type of holiday | *A story about two people falling in love
test: Which word means the feeling of love and excitement between two people? | *Romance | Friendship | Sadness | Ancient
exam: Which meaning fits best in «the romance of the sea»? | *An exciting, mysterious feeling about the sea | A loving couple who live by the sea | A story about a sinking ship | A fact about how deep the sea is
